flowchart TB
    accTitle: What the settings page shows for an answer
    accDescr: The settings page sends a save or Disconnect to Nextcloud and shows one sentence for whatever comes back. When the browser gets no answer, the sentence says that Nextcloud could not be reached. HTTP 401 or 412 means that the session expired, and HTTP 503 that Nextcloud is in maintenance mode. A refusal of the app brings its own message in the language of the administrator. An answer of the app shows the settings as Nextcloud stored them, with the URL in its stored form, and the message of success; anything else, such as the HTML page of a proxy, gives the request failed with its HTTP status. Every message has the colour and the icon of its kind, and Disconnect is on only while a token or a URL is stored.

    send(["`**Test connection and save**<br>or **Disconnect**`"])
    reached{"Does the browser<br>get an answer?"}
    session{"HTTP 401 or 412?"}
    maintenance{"HTTP 503?"}
    app{"JSON of the app?"}
    unreached["Nextcloud could not be reached"]
    expired["Your session has expired"]
    upgrade["Nextcloud is in maintenance mode"]
    refusal["The message of the app,<br>such as Paperless rejected<br>the API token"]
    stored["The settings as stored,<br>the URL in its stored form:<br>Connection successful"]
    failed["The request failed (HTTP 502)"]
    disconnect["Disconnect on only while<br>a token or a URL is stored"]

    send --> reached
    reached -- "no" --> unreached
    reached -- "yes" --> session
    session -- "yes" --> expired
    session -- "no" --> maintenance
    maintenance -- "yes" --> upgrade
    maintenance -- "no" --> app
    app -- "a refusal, with its message" --> refusal
    app -- "the settings" --> stored
    app -- "no, such as the HTML<br>page of a proxy" --> failed
    stored --> disconnect
    refusal --> disconnect

    classDef yes fill:#16a34a2e,stroke:#16a34a,stroke-width:2px
    classDef no fill:#dc26262e,stroke:#dc2626,stroke-width:2px
    class stored yes
    class unreached,expired,upgrade,refusal,failed no
